                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Cold Space is a small science fiction game built around the idea of surviving and exploring in a cold, isolated space environment. The setting gives the experience an immediate feeling of loneliness, with the emptiness around me making every location feel more distant and uncertain. It is more interested in creating a focused sci-fi atmosphere than delivering a massive space adventure.\n\nThe atmosphere is the strongest part for me. Cold environments and empty spaces naturally create a sense of isolation, and the game uses that feeling to make exploration more interesting. I like moving through unfamiliar areas and wondering what I might discover, especially when the surroundings suggest that something has gone wrong.\n\nExploration is also an important part of the experience. I have to look around, investigate different areas and pay attention to environmental details. The slower approach works well because it gives the setting time to create tension rather than rushing me from one objective to another.\n\nThe science fiction presentation gives the game some personality as well. I enjoy the contrast between advanced technology and the harsh, empty environment. Even simple locations can become interesting when they are presented as part of a larger abandoned or isolated space setting.\n\nThe biggest weakness is that the gameplay can feel limited. Once I understand the main exploration mechanics, there may not be enough different activities to keep me engaged for a long time. More puzzles, survival systems or interactive environments could give the experience more depth without taking away from its atmosphere.\n\nThe pacing can also be quite slow. That works when I am in the mood for a quiet atmospheric game, but there are sections where I feel like I am spending a long time moving through an area without enough happening. Players who prefer constant action may find the experience too passive.\n\nThe presentation is effective when it focuses on emptiness and isolation rather than trying to overwhelm me with visual effects. The cold sci-fi setting provides a clear identity, although more environmental variety would make the journey feel more memorable and prevent locations from blending together.\n\nOverall, Cold Space is a small atmospheric sci-fi experience that succeeds mainly through its sense of isolation. I like the exploration, cold futuristic setting and slower pacing, while the limited gameplay variety prevents it from becoming a particularly deep adventure. It is best suited to players who enjoy quiet science fiction experiences where the environment is just as important as the mechanics.\n\nRating: 7.6/10\n",
